<title>SINGAPORE: Indian cancels Vizag Jan 5-7 naphtha sell tender.</title>
<headline>Indian cancels Vizag Jan 5-7 naphtha sell tender.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has cancelled its tender to sell 25,000 tonnes of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) lifting January 5-7 from Vizag on the east coast, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;It was cancelled due to an internal indigenous requirement,&quot; a source said.</p>
<p>The tender closed December 20 and was valid until December 21.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
</text>
